WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.976 --> 00:00:13.436
While Mr.

2
00:00:13.456 --> 00:00:14.857
Bumble was proposing to Mrs.

3
00:00:14.937 --> 00:00:18.078
Corney, Fagin sat brooding in front of his own fire.

4
00:00:19.198 --> 00:00:22.760
At a table behind him, the Artful Dodger played cards with Charley Bates.

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.841
As it was a cold night, the Dodger wore his hat.

6
00:00:27.842 --> 00:00:29.923
He and Charley laughed and joked while they played.

7
00:00:29.943 --> 00:00:32.724
"Hark!" the Dodger cried suddenly.

8
00:00:33.768 --> 00:00:34.569
"I heard the bell."

9
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.732
Taking the only candle, he crept softly upstairs to open the door.

10
00:00:39.813 --> 00:00:44.036
The bell was rung again with some impatience while Fagin and Charley waited below in darkness.

11
00:00:45.297 --> 00:00:48.420
After a short pause, the Dodger reappeared and whispered to Fagin.

12
00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.982
"What!" cried Fagin.

13
00:00:51.983 --> 00:00:52.723
"He's alone?"

14
00:00:53.804 --> 00:00:55.065
The Dodger nodded to Fagin.

15
00:00:56.066 --> 00:00:59.429
He also signaled to Charley that now would not be a good time for joking.

16
00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:03.032
Fagin looked as if he dreaded hearing some terrible news.

17
00:01:04.704 --> 00:01:05.184
"Where is he?"

18
00:01:05.544 --> 00:01:06.105
asked Fagin.

19
00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:08.426
The Dodger pointed upstairs.

20
00:01:08.446 --> 00:01:10.827
"Bring him down immediately."

21
00:01:11.867 --> 00:01:13.047
The Dodger went upstairs.

22
00:01:14.148 --> 00:01:16.649
He returned, followed by a man wearing a heavy coat.

23
00:01:17.769 --> 00:01:22.091
After a hurried glance around the room, the man pulled off a large scarf that had concealed the

24
00:01:22.131 --> 00:01:23.211
lower part of his face.

25
00:01:24.412 --> 00:01:25.492
It was Toby Crackit.

26
00:01:25.512 --> 00:01:27.533
"How are you, Fagin?"

27
00:01:27.853 --> 00:01:28.374
said Toby.

28
00:01:28.394 --> 00:01:31.775
"I can't talk business till I've had something to eat and drink.

29
00:01:32.815 --> 00:01:34.136
I've had nothing for three days."

30
00:01:35.264 --> 00:01:37.726
Fagin signaled for the Dodger to bring some food and drink.

31
00:01:38.747 --> 00:01:40.668
Then he motioned for Toby to sit at the table.

32
00:01:41.869 --> 00:01:45.431
Once the meal arrived, Fagin dismissed the boys and took a seat at the table.

33
00:01:46.532 --> 00:01:49.794
Toby ate his food slowly, in no hurry to tell his story.

34
00:01:50.895 --> 00:01:52.816
Meanwhile Fagin waited in agony.

35
00:01:53.917 --> 00:01:55.658
At last Toby was ready to talk.

36
00:01:56.779 --> 00:01:58.220
He wiped his mouth and stretched.

37
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.103
"First and foremost, Fagin, how's Bill?"

38
00:02:03.284 --> 00:02:05.669
"What?" screamed Fagin, jumping up from his seat.

39
00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:09.891
"Why, you don't mean to say began Toby, turning pale.

40
00:02:09.911 --> 00:02:12.133
"Where are they?"

41
00:02:12.473 --> 00:02:15.074
cried Fagin, stamping his foot furiously on the floor.

42
00:02:15.094 --> 00:02:17.155
"Sikes and the boy!

43
00:02:18.076 --> 00:02:18.956
Where are they hiding?

44
00:02:19.937 --> 00:02:21.137
Why have they not been here?"

45
00:02:21.157 --> 00:02:24.559
"The robbery failed," Toby said faintly.

46
00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:26.821
"Yes, I know that."

47
00:02:27.961 --> 00:02:30.823
Fagin tore a newspaper page from his pocket and pointed to it.

48
00:02:31.983 --> 00:02:32.924
"What else happened?"

49
00:02:34.064 --> 00:02:35.665
"Someone fired a gun and hit the boy.

50
00:02:36.625 --> 00:02:38.605
We ran through the fields carrying him between us.

51
00:02:39.686 --> 00:02:41.086
They gave chase through hedge and ditch.

52
00:02:42.226 --> 00:02:44.507
The whole village was awake, and the dogs were after us."

53
00:02:44.527 --> 00:02:46.448
"And Oliver?"

54
00:02:46.468 --> 00:02:49.268
"His head hung down and he was cold.

55
00:02:51.009 --> 00:02:52.109
They were close on our heels.

56
00:02:53.169 --> 00:02:55.190
It was every man for himself to avoid the gallows!

57
00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:58.671
Bill and I parted company and left the boy lying in a ditch.

58
00:02:59.671 --> 00:03:01.712
Dead or alive, that's all I know about him."

59
00:03:02.796 --> 00:03:04.177
Fagin waited to hear no more.

60
00:03:05.197 --> 00:03:07.639
Uttering a yell, he rushed from the room and from the house.

61
00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.501
The old man reached the street corner.

62
00:03:11.541 --> 00:03:16.204
He was pressing onward in the same wild manner when suddenly a carriage dashed past and forced him

63
00:03:16.324 --> 00:03:17.905
out of the street and onto the pavement.

64
00:03:18.985 --> 00:03:22.387
At last he came to a narrow and dismal alley leading to Saffron Hill.

65
00:03:23.468 --> 00:03:27.110
In its filthy shops were huge bunches of secondhand silk handkerchiefs.

66
00:03:28.251 --> 00:03:29.912
They were of all sizes and patterns.

67
00:03:31.068 --> 00:03:34.450
Hundreds of these handkerchiefs dangled from pegs outside the shop windows.

68
00:03:35.511 --> 00:03:37.792
It was into this part of the city that Fagin turned.

69
00:03:39.533 --> 00:03:43.175
He was well known to the citizens of this alley, who were all in the business of buying

70
00:03:43.195 --> 00:03:44.476
and selling stolen goods.

71
00:03:45.676 --> 00:03:48.858
They nodded familiarly to him as he passed, but he didn't stop.

72
00:03:49.899 --> 00:03:54.141
Fagin was heading for a certain pub, the one where Bill Sikes and his dog could often be

73
00:03:54.201 --> 00:03:59.364
found. At the pub Fagin made a sign to the man at the bar and walked straight upstairs.

74
00:04:00.576 --> 00:04:03.497
He opened the door to a large, dark room that was filled with people.

75
00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:08.178
Looking around anxiously, he seemed to be in search of some particular person.

76
00:04:09.318 --> 00:04:11.699
He beckoned to the landlord and quietly left the room.

77
00:04:11.719 --> 00:04:13.840
"What can I do for you, Mr.

78
00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.801
Fagin?" inquired the man as he followed him out to the landing.

79
00:04:16.821 --> 00:04:18.641
"Won't you join us?"

80
00:04:19.761 --> 00:04:23.202
Fagin shook his head impatiently and whispered, "Is he here?"

81
00:04:23.222 --> 00:04:27.884
"No." "And no news of Bill Sikes either?"

82
00:04:27.904 --> 00:04:30.432
"None," replied the landlord.

83
00:04:30.452 --> 00:04:32.793
"Bill won't stir until it's safe.

84
00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:34.373
Depend on that.

85
00:04:35.354 --> 00:04:39.035
The police are on the scent down there, and if he moved, he'd blow the whole thing."

86
00:04:39.055 --> 00:04:41.376
"Will he be here tonight?"

87
00:04:41.716 --> 00:04:42.456
Fagin asked again.

88
00:04:42.476 --> 00:04:44.256
"Do you mean Monks?"

89
00:04:44.276 --> 00:04:46.557
"Hush," said Fagin.

90
00:04:46.577 --> 00:04:50.298
"Yes." "I expected him before now.

91
00:04:51.279 --> 00:04:55.700
If you'll wait ten minutes, he'll probably "No, no," said Fagin hastily.

92
00:04:56.748 --> 00:04:59.709
"Tell him I was here and that he must come to see me tomorrow night."

93
00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.631
With that, Fagin went downstairs and out into the street.

94
00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:08.513
He hailed a carriage and rode to within a half mile of Bill Sikes' house.

95
00:05:09.733 --> 00:05:11.634
Then he got out and walked the rest of the way.

96
00:05:12.775 --> 00:05:15.396
He arrived to find no one at Bill Sikes' house but Nancy.

97
00:05:17.057 --> 00:05:18.897
She was sleeping with her head upon the table.

98
00:05:19.978 --> 00:05:21.418
She looked up as he closed the door.

99
00:05:21.438 --> 00:05:24.239
"Where do you think Bill is now, my dear?"

100
00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:25.160
asked Fagin.

101
00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.722
"I can't say," muttered Nancy, laying her head back down on the table.

102
00:05:30.863 --> 00:05:33.324
Fagin told her everything he'd learned from Toby Crackit.

103
00:05:33.344 --> 00:05:34.985
"And Oliver.

104
00:05:35.985 --> 00:05:36.866
Poor little boy.

105
00:05:37.866 --> 00:05:39.027
Left in a ditch, Nancy!"

106
00:05:39.047 --> 00:05:43.850
"The boy is better off where he is," said Nancy, suddenly looking up.

107
00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:48.932
"And if no harm comes to Bill from it, I hope Oliver lies dead in that ditch."

108
00:05:50.093 --> 00:05:52.014
"What?" cried Fagin in amazement.

109
00:05:52.034 --> 00:05:55.576
"Yes, I do," said Nancy, meeting his gaze.

110
00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:59.862
"I shall be glad to have him out of my sight and to know that the worst is

111
00:05:59.962 --> 00:06:02.663
over. I can't bear to have him near me.

112
00:06:03.624 --> 00:06:06.265
The sight of him turns me against myself and all of you."

113
00:06:06.285 --> 00:06:12.469
"If Sikes comes back and leaves the boy behind, dead or alive Fagin said angrily.

114
00:06:12.489 --> 00:06:14.550
"What's all this about?"

115
00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:15.571
cried Nancy.

116
00:06:15.591 --> 00:06:19.693
"That boy's worth hundreds of pounds to me," raged Fagin.

117
00:06:19.713 --> 00:06:26.788
"And I'm bound to someone, a devil that only wants the will and has the power to Suddenly

118
00:06:26.828 --> 00:06:28.849
he stopped and his whole demeanor changed.

119
00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:34.893
He unclenched his fists and sank quietly into a chair as if afraid that he'd revealed too much.

120
00:06:36.114 --> 00:06:38.975
"Nancy, dear," said Fagin in his usual voice.

121
00:06:38.995 --> 00:06:41.096
"Don't bother me now.

122
00:06:41.116 --> 00:06:42.937
I want to sleep.

123
00:06:43.978 --> 00:06:46.719
If Toby got away, Bill's pretty sure to be safe too."

124
00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:48.520
"And the boy?"

125
00:06:49.581 --> 00:06:51.282
Briefly Nancy raised her head again.

126
00:06:51.302 --> 00:06:54.524
"He'll have to take his chances with the rest of them."
